From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: H96 build <builder@h96-build>
Date: Mon, 19 Oct 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 20/59] arm64: dts: rockchip: h96-max-v58: DDR DVFS off (dmc
 and dfi disabled)

On the 6.1 kernel with the 8.0 DTB the dfi probe fails ("Failed to get
pclk_ddr_mon_ch0", -22) and dmc stays in deferred probe forever, so the
DDR rate never changes after the loader. On 6.12 both probe and devfreq
moves DDR between 1560 and 2112 MHz through ATF 0x100 ("unsupported
get_stall_time"). 6.12 t1 and t2 froze between about 13 and 28 s uptime
with no kernel record; DMC is the first proven behaviour difference.

Disable both nodes (rk3588-android.dtsi enables them) so 6.12 keeps the
6.1 effective behaviour. Bisect step t3.
---
 arch/arm64/boot/dts/rockchip/rk3588-h96-max-v58.dts | 9 +++++++++
 1 file changed, 9 insertions(+)

diff --git a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/rockchip/rk3588-h96-max-v58.dts b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/rockchip/rk3588-h96-max-v58.dts
index 863af8161..aa3702c22 100644
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/rockchip/rk3588-h96-max-v58.dts
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/rockchip/rk3588-h96-max-v58.dts
@@ -521,6 +521,15 @@ &vop {
 	/delete-property/ vop-supply;
 };
 
+/* DDR DVFS off: on 6.1 dfi fails (no pclk_ddr_mon_ch0) and dmc never probes, DDR rate stays as set by loader */
+&dfi {
+	status = "disabled";
+};
+
+&dmc {
+	status = "disabled";
+};
+
 /* AV1 decoder and its IOMMU */
 &av1d {
 	status = "okay";
